npm run verify:notification-permission-ssot-contract
node scripts/qa/notification-receive-gate-adb-qa.mjs
```

## Legacy Receive Policy (3-tier — do not mix)

Full doc: `docs/permissions/dibay-legacy-call-receive-policy.md`

- **DIBAY only:** Runtime official gate = `receiveReady` (Notification). Do **not** state this as universal legacy-app law.
- **Runtime tier:** Notification → FCM → Runtime → Ring → Incoming UI. FSI/mic/camera/battery/speaker/bluetooth **must not** block Runtime.
- **Lock Screen tier:** FSI/battery → lock full UI only; Runtime/Ring/Incoming UI **continue**.
- **Media tier:** Mic/Camera at accept/outgoing gesture → Join only; **must not** block receive.
  - iOS (Owner 2026-11-08 「텔레그램 방식」): Mic/Camera asked **only** at call gesture (never at login). Not-determined → OS prompt with **no timeout** (wait for the user's answer). Denied (now or already) → outgoing does not start / incoming accept ends the call, then `DibayCallPermissionSettingsPrompt` (alert with Settings button; local notification when backgrounded). Notification/ringing receive itself is not gated by mic/camera. Android keeps its own flow (ringing continues + settings).
  - iOS build 27 (Owner 2026-11-08 lock-screen answer): incoming accept with Not-determined (and nothing denied) → **connect first**, then ask mic (→ camera for video) via `DibayDeferredCallMediaPermission` when the app becomes active (unlock / open app). Deny then → end call + `DibayCallPermissionSettingsPrompt`. Already denied at accept → end immediately + prompt. Outgoing unchanged.
  - iOS post-login (Owner 2026-11-08 「그래」 — supersedes 「never at login」 above): after the notification OS prompt, `requestPostLoginCallMediaOsPermissions` shows the mic → camera **OS** prompts (no app screen, only not-yet-asked ones), so calls received on the lock screen already have permission. Reason: iOS cannot show permission prompts over the lock screen. The build 27 deferred path stays as the fallback.
- **Invariant:** Permission UX changes **must not** modify Runtime, FCM, Agora, Native Runtime, `NotificationReceiveGate`.
- Post-login FSI (Android): `runPostLoginFullScreenIntentCheck()` — FSI off → `openFullScreenIntentSettings()` direct, no DIBAY modal. Resume/visibility: sync only.
